BEFORE the callback fix
-----------------------
Legacy diagnostic log analysis: 238 of 269 generations ended at exactly 28,800
samples (1.2 s at 24 kHz), i.e. the first 15-frame Kokoro chunk. Sentences were
therefore cut mid-phrase at a nearly constant duration. The callback returned 0
(stop) after a successful write; sherpa-onnx's contract is 1=continue, 0=stop.

AFTER the callback fix (final build)
------------------------------------
13:43:31.181  adblock ready network=122884 cosmetic=32403 scriptlets=4612 build=365ms skipped=527
13:43:38.352  play started engine=sherpa sentence=0/108
13:43:42.139  gen done "Chapter 67: Who is he?" in 3789ms frames=79975
13:43:56.814  gen done "The teaching faculty provide" in 10233ms frames=385360
13:44:08.488  gen done "Although none of them had ou" in 11663ms frames=634086
13:44:20.045  gen done "The only thing they couldn't" in 11540ms frames=865829
13:44:25.313  gen done "“You should have seen his en" in 5249ms frames=966309
13:44:37.141  gen done "He came running in, pushed I" in 11814ms frames=1185131
13:44:42.212  gen done "He was like a hero who came " in 5049ms frames=1277514

`frames` is the cumulative PcmPlayer writtenFrames. The first 3.3 s sentence alone
emitted 80,002 samples; generation continued through the chapter instead of
stopping at the 28,800-sample chunk.

